getAnglesTable [SimTalk]
Returns the Angles Table of the PickAndPlace robot designated by <Path> and writes it into a table.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.getAnglesTable(AnglesTable:table) -> table
Parameter
The parameter AnglesTable of data type table designates the name of the table.
It contains:
• The Name of the predecessor at which the PickAndPlace robot picks the part up or the Name of the
successor onto which the PickAndPlace robot deposits the part.
The column Name can also contain a sensor on the Conveyor, for example Conveyor.sensorID(1).
• The Angle between the station in the column Name and the PickAndPlace robot.
getAnglesTable [SimTalk]
11-1936 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

If you insert Connectors or if you drag an object onto the PickAndPlace robot and drop it there, Plant
Simulation adds the respective values to the angles table. If you delete a Connector, Plant Simulation does
not remove the respective entry from the table. You have to do this manually.
You can also manually change values or names in the angles table or add new stations to it. This way you
can, for example, request the PickAndPlace robot in a Sensor Control.
Note
Plant Simulation automatically applies changed names of stations to the Times Table.
Return Value
The return value has the data type table.
Example
var myAnglesTable: table
MyPickAndPlace.getAnglesTable(myAnglesTable)
SimTalk
